                <pb facs="0068" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1825: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Counselor of
                        Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Chungking</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-29T18:00:00-04:00">May 29, 1939—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. Department’s 90, May 19, 6 p.m., last paragraph, and your 341, May 23, 10
                    a.m. On May 29 an officer of the Department took this matter up with the Chinese
                    Ambassador here and gave him a copy of our text of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> which you delivered to the Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    on May 22.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
